{"ad":{"id":"fdff6eb7-e545-409c-831d-3b70891b4667","word":"AD","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"anno Domini — see also CE","word":"DC"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"anno Domini — see also CE","word":"d.C. (depois de Cristo)"}],"pos":"adv","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"They had a vibrant culture from the 3rd century BC to the 2nd century AD.","bold_text_offsets":[[70,72]],"type":"example","id":"352881fd-dc40-4b2a-8a6a-16a8414f72b8"},{"text":"Today is 15 May AD 2026.","bold_text_offsets":[[16,18]],"type":"example","id":"7ee3df4f-524a-4448-aa16-7074d1814c05"},{"text":"Founded Aᴼ.Dᴵ. 1728 by Benj. Franklin","ref":"1916 September 23, The Saturday Evening Post, volume 189, number 13, page 3:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[8,14]],"id":"6ba2efc5-52d5-4d71-84af-db78d7b4e03d"},{"text":"There is a striving towards naturalism in agricultural scenes painted on bricks in tombs of the third century AD recently excavated at Chia-yü-kuan in Kansu Province which is reminiscent of later European illuminated manuscripts such as the English fifteenth-century Luttrell Psalter in the British Library.","ref":"1979, Paul Hulton, Lawrence Smith, “Naturalism in Sung China”, in Flowers in Art from East and West, Jarrold and Sons, →ISBN, →OCLC, page 3:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[110,112]],"id":"978d058a-66f8-459e-b294-002c9b66160b"},{"text":"But keep on the lookout for the 1st-century-a.d. stele on the right wall, with symbols of the deceased’s civic scribely duties (a scroll and codex), and the fresco remnants around to the left.","ref":"2010, John Moretti, “Perugia, Assisi & Northern Umbria”, in Florence, Tuscany & Umbria (Frommer’s), 7th edition, Wiley Publishing, Inc., →ISBN, section 2 (Assisi: An Artistic Pilgrimage), page 393:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[44,48]],"id":"6781aadc-e7af-449f-8baa-712952fdd4b1"}],"categories":["English initialisms","English terms with quotation